1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:11,800
Before the dawn of creation, Sree Maha Vishu rested upon Ananta in cosmic contemplation.
When cosmic order wavers, Sree Maha Vishu descends.

2
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:20,800
As the great deluge dissolved the world, Matsya the Divine Fish guided the sacred ark,
preserving life and the eternal Vedas.

3
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:30,800
As gods and demons churned the cosmic ocean, Kurma the Divine Tortoise
bore Mount Mandara to steady creation.

4
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:39,500
Plunging into the dark abyss, Varaha lifted Mother Earth upon His divine tusks,
restoring Her to eternal light.

5
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:48,200
Bursting forth from the stone pillar, the fierce Man-Lion Narasimha
destroyed tyranny and shielded unwavering devotion.

6
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:57,200
Measuring the universe in three strides, the humble youth Vamana taught
that true humility surpasses earthly power.

7
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:06,200
Wielding the sacred battle-axe, Parashurama punished corrupt tyranny
and decreed power must serve righteousness.

8
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:15,200
Mariyada Purushottama Sri Rama sacrificed all worldly comfort,
proving that righteousness must triumph at any cost.

9
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:24,200
Upon the battlefield of Kurukshetra, Bhagavan Krishna unveiled the Bhagavad Gita,
the immortal light of divine wisdom.

10
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:33,200
Forsaking the illusions of power and war, Buddha illuminated the path
of inner peace, boundless compassion, and truth.

11
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:42,200
Riding the blazing white steed Devadatta, Kalki descends
to conquer darkness and herald the golden dawn of renewal.

12
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:55,000
Ten divine descents across the cosmic wheel of time.
Sree Maha Vishu protects the universe. Dharma will rise again. Om Namo Narayanaya.

